{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383641} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7c5b80-cf72-50b6-beaf-a55cb5a4e731" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22bcbd45-a248-5b85-8643-997aed86120a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383647} {:answer/id #uuid "6a012830-1859-5376-b78c-b5ce93fc2b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383648} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ef4af6-694c-5da8-b4a7-045385e71bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383649} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8c9e4b-6ad1-5568-8838-c14f8064fb2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383650} {:answer/id #uuid "318d1154-0e6f-5b9b-9567-fa06e0f161e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7ef4af6-694c-5da8-b4a7-045385e71bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383649} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c14e5c-4f2d-5c9e-8b56-99780514402e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc6d9b64-fae9-5e89-abfa-9eb8e573a546" :question/math-academy-id "q-181683" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2591e9da960008980cf96184975ef19713735814183a97ca8c8f784536fced5.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x-3\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+4}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x-3$ and *below* the line $y=x+4.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x-3,\\,y<x+4.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x-3<y<x+4.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=-x-3$ and $y=x+4$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n-x-3\\le y\\le x+4\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x-3\\le y\\le x+4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0f3e55-2f5d-5cc2-a6c2-4ec49f624ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285196} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e5ef37-95f1-50b2-b2c2-51e62aac2eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286257} {:answer/id #uuid "a9222ec9-3dd0-55a9-9265-77dc50ccbf7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286329} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e31e4b-076f-5d73-9576-e17fe67ed983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286483} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ac85f9-a507-5bb1-adb0-45d76fb0c3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value