/ref 17592186285021} {:answer/id #uuid "2b21ed84-2539-540a-b2c9-c5f03b4c5b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285164} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4e136d-79f8-52ff-97ec-9a19d7996f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285773} {:answer/id #uuid "9aae4206-4cc5-5d8c-a3cf-54947d9cc37c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286204} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c27c52-4bfa-51d9-9227-18829d6cf23a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b21ed84-2539-540a-b2c9-c5f03b4c5b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285164} :answer-field/id #uuid "98e0b1a0-f703-5540-ba59-794d5a028b2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ec6a93c-1a73-5b19-bbef-75f3b804c771" :question/math-academy-id "q-181690" :question/problem "![](images/88/883d270ae063f134ee0ac04f717bcc9b5800adb939be3c7f19f25602ad52360e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-2\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-2$ and *below* the line $y=2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-2,\\,y<2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-2<y<2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=2$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n-2<y\\le 2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<y\\le 2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227f77c6-ffec-582e-a761-f4de9b4799f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/4535a7c6aa7fe8f358d3463b4654c735e53df373d1001916dc035290ca54f969.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285097} {:answer/id #uuid "28e4b2b6-f535-5d78-873b-29236664da4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7a/7ae3c488e60d3dcda304649e575a7d2efc54be7262a54d0455550af420c39b68.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285146} {:answer/id #uuid "ab95ab01-9bf1-569d-adc3-b5dbdacd80f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/9303385b85b1bedfa6add9933b1953a0cdc74581c0f69ffed4d4ad3f0a113bf1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286356} {:answer/id #uuid "cf15457c-b369-5a8b-8e09-c743087e1687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c0/c0df23ec47d729f597c02acff1530dd646a6f6c506a6497a8cb4d75b7fce5e74.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286668} {:answer/id #uuid "fff0f9f4-26ca-5cc7-9aec-5a5e9377ef1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/146139f4429b4b864a027a263abe7a6133b5b96c48aae37d5f9bc1a3635263ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf15457c-b369-5a8b-8e09-c743087e1687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c0/c0df23ec47d729f597c02acff1530dd646a6f6c506a6497a8cb4d75b7fce5e74.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286668} :answer-field/id #uuid "268413d0-7364-50bc-b648-15d4e195ccd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4fc5e64b-6205-5324-9efb-c4a7ebedcc24" :question/math-academy-id "q-181779" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times R$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times R\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/06/067b3b386273b09d5614f934f6525bd3e43ff46f420eb8aa7e744f635ff6d101.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a8/a870f65350ad00d258471079a34bec49a47d331c176dc7a91b3c7aae5ae968dd.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $R\\times N$ as the set of vertical lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0df23ec47d729f597c02acff1530dd646a6f6c506a6497a8cb4d75b7fce5e74.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2260bf3c-77e6-5897-990a-333cd179935e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285094} {:answer/id #uuid "71990b00-4802-52dd-8df2-3b058fb38cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285831} {:answer/id #uuid "81f49580-4c64-5862-a9cc-1d7ecd843e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285980} {:answer/id #uuid "83dc704e-7ed2-5651-8d18-8e77384252e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285998} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3ff751-52c4-5e98-914e-4579de28d363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286491} {:answer/id #uuid "efe1a97f-9f17-5269-9f19-f71f50df904d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efe1a97f-9f17-5269-9f19-f71f50df904d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286989} :answer-field/id #uuid "42787659-cf37-56e3-b091-e82a759db14c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-fiel